  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1000 PM CDT Sat Sep 5 2026\n\nTuesday through Saturday:\n\nQuiet start to the extended period is generally expected for\nTuesday with high pressure likely holding on through the day\nTuesday though conditions suggest that hotter and humid\nconditions should return as a southerly moist flow returns. \nInto Tuesday evening expect a low pressure system lifting \nthrough south central Canada to drag a front through southern \nWI. An additional low pressure forming over the southwest US \nwill also likely extend a warm frontal feature creating somewhat\nof a stationary front slowly progressing east. There is \nuncertainty on exactly where things line up and the timing and \nprogression but most models suggest the impact of this system is\nnot expected to persist beyond Wednesday. This should bring \nstorm chances and rain to the region especially given the decent\nupper level shortwave energy in combination with some help from\nthe LLJ at least for Tuesday night. Into Thursday, uncertainty \nincreases in the surface fields but in general given dry upper \nlevel fields despite a shortwave rolling through we could \npotentially see another dry day though the moisture trends are \nworth watching given that increase moisture aloft could allow \nfor precip. Into Friday and beyond weak flow will potentially \nyield active weather possibly through the late week period into \nthe weekend depending on how the forcing and moisture unfold but\nit will be worth monitoring through the midweek period when we \nshould expect a better idea of how things will go.\n\nKuroski",
